**What changed**

`swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift` — added:
- `public enum NoteParseError: Error, Equatable { case malformedFormat }`
- `public func parseNote(from text: String) throws -> Note`

The parser splits on the literal `\n---\n` (with `omittingEmptySubsequences: false` so empty fields still count), requires exactly 4 parts, maps them to `id`, `title`, `pinned`, `body` in that order, parses `pinned` from `"1"`/`"0"` (rejecting anything else), and builds tags via the existing `extractTags(from:)`. Any other part count, empty string, or invalid pinned value throws `NoteParseError.malformedFormat`.

`swift/Tests/NoteKitTests/NoteKitTests.swift` — added 5 tests covering a valid 4-field parse (including tag extraction), an unpinned note, and the three malformed cases (wrong field count, empty string, bad pinned value).

